\maketitle
\section{The document interface}
A host creates an engine with \texttt{lmtex.new()} and passes source to
\texttt{engine:compile(source, device)}. The returned string is binary-safe.
\section{Persistent fragments}
Use \texttt{engine:fragment(source, device)} to keep definitions between
submissions. A full compilation starts a fresh document.
\section{Errors and ownership}
Compilation errors return nil and diagnostic text. The engine is collected
automatically; \texttt{engine:close()} also releases it explicitly.
